.TH SYNORA-COMPANION 1 "June 2026" "Synora Studio 1.0" "Synora Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
synora-companion \- Synora Studio Headless Administration Toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B companion_operation.py
[\-\-headless] [\-\-action \fIACTION\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B synora-companion
is the core administration toolkit for Synora Studio. It provides utilities for SaaS database migration, tenant provisioning, network configuration, and destructive platform maintenance. When run without the \fB\-\-headless\fR flag, it launches an interactive PySide6 graphical interface. 
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-headless, \-\-cli
Execute the toolkit in headless mode. Useful for automated remote deployments and SSH administration.
.TP
.B \-\-action \fIACTION\fR
Specifies an automated action to execute.
Available actions: \fBbackup\fR, \fBcreate-user\fR, \fBweb-config\fR, \fBdanger-zone\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-demo-user
Injects a pre-verified 'demo@grid.net' demonstration account into the live SaaS database.
Used natively with \fB\-\-action create-user\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-delete-demo-user
Removes the 'demo@grid.net' demonstration account.
Used natively with \fB\-\-action create-user\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-username \fIUSER\fR
Username for tenant creation. Defaults to demo_user.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
Password for tenant creation.
.TP
.B \-\-bypass-otp
Injects the OTP bypass flag into the tenant's security blob, skipping the email verification requirement.
.TP
.B \-\-target-dir \fIDIR\fR
Target directory for SaaS local SQLite database backups.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch interactive CLI menu:
.B python companion_operation.py --headless
.TP
Inject demo user headlessly:
.B python companion_operation.py --headless --action create-user --demo-user
.TP
Wipe all platform tenants (Danger Zone):
.B python companion_operation.py --headless --action danger-zone
.SH AUTHOR
Synora Studio Framework
